// The README of each generated package: what it holds and how a product consumes it.
import type { Model } from "../model.ts";
import { title } from "./figma.ts";

const HEADER =
  "<!-- GENERATED by nddev-opennetwork-design-system (`just generate`). Edit src/emit/readmes.ts. -->\n\n";

export function readmes(model: Model): Map<string, string> {
  const directions = model.registry.directions
    .map((d) => `\`${d.id}\``)
    .join(", ");
  const themes = model.themes.map((t) => `\`${t.id}\``).join(", ");
  const out = new Map<string, string>();
  const vendoring =
    "Consume a release: copy this directory from the tag `vX.Y.Z` into the product and record the tag and the directory digest (docs/adr/0001-architecture.md §13). Never edit the copy; update it from a newer tag.";

  out.set(
    "web/README.md",
    `${HEADER}# OpenNetwork design tokens — web

- \`tokens.css\`: every token as a custom property in \`@layer tokens\` (\`--surface-base\`, \`--accent-on-fill\`, \`--text-size-h1\`). Context comes from attributes on any element, nested freely:
  - \`data-theme\`: ${themes} (default \`${model.defaults["theme"] ?? ""}\`);
  - \`data-direction\`: ${directions} (default \`${model.defaults["direction"] ?? ""}\`);
  - \`data-platform="desktop"\` in desktop webviews (Tauri, Electron): fixed, denser type and pointer-sized controls;
  - \`data-density="compact"\`;
  - \`data-motion="reduced"\` or \`"standard"\` (without it, \`prefers-reduced-motion\` decides).
- \`kit.css\`: the UI kit (\`@layer base\` and \`@layer primitives\`): every implemented component of \`kit/components/\` as \`nd-*\` classes over the tokens, including the global focus ring, reduced motion and forced colours. The product declares the order of the layers. Mark a region whose own width should decide how components fit (a card column, a sidebar) with \`.nd-container\` (CSS container queries); give it a width from its layout, since it no longer sizes to its content.
- \`text-styles.css\`: the kit's text styles as \`.nd-text-<role>\` classes, with the script rules (Arabic and Chinese families, no tracking or case, their body leading) by \`:lang()\`. Headings balance their lines and running text avoids a lone last word (\`text-wrap\`). It also declares the fallback face the family stacks name: a local Arial scaled to Plex's advance and vertical metrics, so the swap to the web font moves a line as little as possible.
- \`reference.html\`: every colour role, text style, script, icon and component with its spec, switchable by theme, direction, platform, density and motion. Run \`node scripts/serve.ts\` from the installed repository and open \`http://127.0.0.1:4870/reference.html\`; this serves the bundled font files without an external font service.
- \`reference-fonts.css\`: the reference page's font faces from the canonical manifest. Products serve those manifest files at their own asset paths; this review stylesheet is not a product font installer.
- \`icons.json\`: the icons and the brand mark to inline (\`viewBox\` and \`body\`).
- \`tokens.json\`: the registry (themes with schemes, directions, platforms), brand seeds, breakpoints in px and rem (custom properties cannot be used in media queries), the kit's text styles by property, and every public token with its property, owner, description and default value.

The page maps \`prefers-contrast: more\` to the contrast themes (\`registry.contrastThemes\`) and \`prefers-color-scheme\` to \`registry.systemThemes\`.

Nested contexts retain the nearest explicit theme/direction and platform/density in browsers with CSS \`@scope\` (Baseline March 2026). Declaring the default web platform, comfortable density or standard motion also restores that context after an inherited override. Flat selectors remain for older engines; they do not establish correct palettes through contradictory nested contexts. \`just test-browser\` runs the reference page, the accessibility trees and the context suite in Chromium, Firefox and WebKit.

${vendoring}
`,
  );
  out.set(
    "apple/README.md",
    `${HEADER}# OpenNetworkDesignTokens — Swift (iOS, iPadOS, macOS)

A Swift package: \`OpenNetworkDesignTokens\` holds every value with no dependency (it builds and tests on Linux too); \`SwiftUI.swift\` adds the bindings where SwiftUI exists.

\`\`\`swift
import OpenNetworkDesignTokens

RootView()
    .ndTheme(.light, direction: .on, platform: .ios, density: .comfortable)

struct Title: View {
    @Environment(\\.ndColors) private var colors
    var body: some View {
        Text("NDDev").ndText(.h1).foregroundStyle(colors.textPrimary.color)
    }
}
\`\`\`

- Colours: \`NDColors.resolve(theme:direction:)\` (sRGB). Increase Contrast (\`colorSchemeContrast == .increased\`) selects \`.darkContrast\` / \`.lightContrast\`.
- Metrics in points: \`NDMetrics.resolve(platform:density:)\`; targets are 44 pt on iOS.
- Text: \`NDTextStyle.resolve(_:platform:script:)\` scales with the Dynamic Type style it names; set \`\\.ndScript\` from the locale (Arabic and Chinese drop tracking and case).
- Motion: \`NDDurations\` take \`.reduced\` when Reduce Motion is on (\`accessibilityReduceMotion\`).
- Icons and the mark: \`NDVectorImage(.arrow)\`, \`NDVectorImage(NDBrand.mark)\` draw in the foreground style, fitted to their frame (decorative, hidden from accessibility).
- Fonts: the package bundles IBM Plex Sans and IBM Plex Sans Arabic (400, 500, 600; OFL-1.1, licence in \`Fonts/\`); call \`NDBundledFonts.register()\` once at launch. Chinese and monospace use the system faces (PingFang SC; SF Mono, else Menlo).
- Tint: where system chrome tints its material or selection (\`.tint\`), it takes the direction's \`accent.brand\`; text and icons on system materials keep the system label colours (ADR 0006).

${vendoring}
`,
  );
  out.set(
    "kotlin/README.md",
    `${HEADER}# OpenNetwork design tokens — Kotlin (Android, Compose Multiplatform desktop)

- \`ai.nddev.opennetwork.design.tokens\`: every value, no dependency (colours ARGB, dimensions dp, text sp).
- \`ai.nddev.opennetwork.design.compose\`: \`NDDevTheme\` maps the roles onto Material 3 (colour scheme and typography) and provides \`LocalNDColors\`, \`LocalNDMetrics\`, \`LocalNDPlatform\`, \`LocalNDScript\`.

\`\`\`kotlin
NDDevTheme(theme = NDTheme.Light, direction = NDDirection.On, families = { appFonts(it) }) {
    Text("NDDev", style = MaterialTheme.typography.headlineLarge, color = LocalNDColors.current.textPrimary.toCompose())
}
\`\`\`

- Fonts: IBM Plex Sans and IBM Plex Sans Arabic (OFL-1.1) are class-path resources listed by \`NDBundledFonts\`; Compose desktop loads them with \`Font(resource = …)\`, an Android app copies them into \`res/font\` (lower-case names). Chinese and monospace use the system faces.
- Android: add \`src/main/kotlin\` to a module's sources and depend on \`androidx.compose.material3:material3\` (the same API). The contrast themes follow \`UiModeManager.getContrast()\`; \`NDMotion.Reduced\` follows an animator duration scale of 0.
- Icons and the mark: \`Icon(NDIcon.Arrow.imageVector, contentDescription = null, tint = …)\`; \`NDBrand.mark.toImageVector("nddev", 48.dp)\`.
- Shapes: \`NDDevTheme\` passes \`ndShapes(metrics)\` to \`MaterialTheme\`, so Material components take the kit's field, chip, card and dialog radii (ADR 0006).
- Desktop: include this directory as a Gradle build (\`build.gradle.kts\` compiles it against Compose Multiplatform Material 3 and runs the tests).

${vendoring}
`,
  );
  out.set(
    "flutter/README.md",
    `${HEADER}# nddev_opennetwork_design_system — Flutter (mobile and desktop)

\`\`\`yaml
dependencies:
  nddev_opennetwork_design_system:
    path: third_party/nddev_opennetwork_design_system
\`\`\`

\`\`\`dart
MaterialApp(
  theme: ndThemeData(theme: NDTheme.light, direction: NDDirection.on),
  darkTheme: ndThemeData(theme: NDTheme.dark, direction: NDDirection.on),
  highContrastTheme: ndThemeData(theme: NDTheme.lightContrast, direction: NDDirection.on),
  highContrastDarkTheme: ndThemeData(theme: NDTheme.darkContrast, direction: NDDirection.on),
  home: const Home(),
);
// In a widget: context.ndColors.accentText, context.ndMetrics.sizeTargetMin
\`\`\`

- Text styles: \`NDTextStyle.resolve(role, platform, script).toTextStyle(platform)\`; upper-case styles (\`uppercase\`) are applied to the string, Flutter has no text transform.
- Motion: pass \`NDMotion.reduced\` to \`NDDurations\` when \`MediaQuery.disableAnimationsOf(context)\` is true.
- Icons and the mark: \`NDVectorIcon.icon(NDIcon.arrow)\` in the ambient icon colour, \`NDVectorIcon(NDBrand.mark, size: 48, color: …)\`.
- Fonts: IBM Plex Sans and IBM Plex Sans Arabic are this package's font assets (OFL-1.1) and the text styles use them; Chinese and monospace use the system faces.
- Shapes: \`ndThemeData\` gives Material's cards, dialogs, bottom sheets, popup menus and chips the kit's radii (a pill radius becomes a stadium).

${vendoring}
`,
  );
  out.set(
    "rust/README.md",
    `${HEADER}# nddev-opennetwork-design-tokens — Rust

A \`no_std\` crate with no dependencies for native desktop interfaces (egui, iced, Slint), image rendering and tools. Every set is a \`static\`; resolving allocates nothing.

\`\`\`rust
use nddev_opennetwork_design_system::{Colors, Direction, Metrics, Platform, Density, Theme, TextStyle, TypeRole, Script};

let colors = Colors::resolve(Theme::Dark, Direction::On);
let metrics = Metrics::resolve(Platform::Desktop, Density::Comfortable);
let h1 = TextStyle::resolve(TypeRole::H1, Platform::Desktop, Script::Latin);
let [r, g, b, a] = colors.accent_text.to_f32();
let arrow = Icon::Arrow.vector(); // SVG path data per shape, for kurbo, lyon or usvg
\`\`\`

\`\`\`toml
[dependencies]
nddev-opennetwork-design-tokens = { path = "third_party/nddev-opennetwork-design-tokens", features = ["fonts"] }
\`\`\`

The \`fonts\` feature adds \`font_files::ALL\`: the TTF bytes of IBM Plex Sans and IBM Plex Sans Arabic (OFL-1.1) for renderers that load fonts from memory.

${vendoring}
`,
  );
  out.set(
    "fonts/README.md",
    `${HEADER}# NDDev fonts

\`manifest.json\` is the contract for every product: the families, the token each serves, the scripts it covers and its licence (all OFL-1.1).

- **Web**: install the exact \`@fontsource\` packages the manifest names, serve the listed WOFF2 files (each checked by its SHA-256) as \`@font-face\` rules with their \`unicode-range\`, preload the files of a script's first view (\`preload\`), and load \`text-styles.css\`, which declares the fallback face (\`fallback\`: Arial scaled so the swap to Plex moves a line as little as possible).
- **Native**: \`ttf/\` holds IBM Plex Sans and IBM Plex Sans Arabic at 400, 500 and 600 from IBM's release (digests in the manifest, licence alongside). The Swift, Kotlin, Flutter and Rust packages bundle the same files. Chinese uses the system CJK face on native platforms (PingFang SC, Noto Sans CJK): Noto Sans SC would add some 17 MB to an app.

${vendoring}
`,
  );
  out.set(
    "icons/README.md",
    `${HEADER}# NDDev icons

The icons of the design, exported from the Figma frames and reduced to geometry: \`svg/<name>.svg\` (paths in \`currentColor\`, the root \`fill="none"\`), \`icons.json\` with each one's viewBox, origin set, licence (MIT, Apache-2.0 or ISC) and frame. Icons are decorative: the control around one carries its meaning, so they are hidden from assistive technology.

Native packages draw the same geometry without image files: SwiftUI \`NDVectorImage\`, Compose \`NDIcon.imageVector\`, Flutter \`NDVectorIcon\`, Rust \`Icon::vector()\`; the web inlines \`packages/web/icons.json\`.

${vendoring}
`,
  );
  out.set(
    "brand/README.md",
    `${HEADER}# NDDev brand

- \`mark.svg\`: the owner's NDDev mark (three polygons), drawn in the direction's colour. It is never redrawn, traced or replaced by a lettering.
- \`icons/<direction>.svg\`: the favicon and direction icon, one style for every direction: a square tile with rounded corners, light by default (the main theme) and dark under \`prefers-color-scheme: dark\`, the mark in the direction's seed where it holds 3:1 on the tile (WCAG 1.4.11), otherwise that theme's \`accent.heading\`.
- \`icons/<direction>-light.svg\`, \`icons/<direction>-dark.svg\`: the two fixed versions; touch icons, the ICO and preview cards are drawn from the light one.
- \`brand.json\`: the seeds, both icon styles and the rasters products draw from the light icon (192 and 180 px icons, a 16/32/48 px ICO, a 1200×630 card with the mark at 300 px).

Native packages carry the mark as geometry (\`NDBrand.mark\`).

${vendoring}
`,
  );
  out.set(
    "figma/README.md",
    `${HEADER}# NDDev Figma library — data

\`variables.json\` is the library file "NDDev Design System" as data; the file is built from it and never edited by hand.

| Collection | Modes | Holds |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Primitives | Value | foundation: space, rhythm, radius, sizes, borders, opacity, leading, tracking, weights, layout |
| Theme | ${model.themes.map((t) => title(t.id)).join(", ")} | every theme role; \`accent/*\` and other direction-dependent roles alias the Direction collection |
| Direction | ${model.registry.directions.map((d) => d.name).join(", ")} | hidden per-theme entries (\`<theme>/accent/text\`) the Theme collection aliases |
| Platform | ${model.modifier("platform").contexts.map(title).join(", ")} | type sizes, font families, hidden per-density control sizes |
| Density | ${model.modifier("density").contexts.map(title).join(", ")} | control and target sizes (aliases into Platform) |
| Motion | ${model.modifier("motion").contexts.map(title).join(", ")} | durations (ms) |
| Component | Value | UI kit roles aliasing semantic and foundation tokens |

A frame picks one mode per collection; theme and direction (and platform and density) compose like the token resolver. Colours are the values native code draws (modifiers applied). Opacity variables are percentages (0-100), the scale Figma applies to layer opacity; the tokens and CSS are 0-1. Effect styles bind each shadow layer to Theme variables; text styles bind family, size and weight to variables and carry leading and tracking as percentages. Web-only values (breakpoints, layered gradients, z-index, springs) stay in code.
`,
  );
  return out;
}
